      "title": "Roformer \u2014 Stem Separation",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Roformer \u2014 Stem Separation\n\nMusic source separation with the [pcunwa Roformer checkpoints](https://huggingface.co/pcunwa/models) (41 checkpoints: the 13 pcunwa releases plus community releases, all 44.1 kHz stereo RoFormers).\n\n**Loader**\n- `model`: any checkpoint id, or a folder in `models/roformer` holding a `.ckpt` plus its config YAML. Weights auto-download from Hugging Face into `models/roformer` on first use (45 MB-1.7 GB).\n- `device`: `auto` (ComfyUI's device), `cuda`, `mps`, `cpu`.\n- `stems` (output): the model's stem names as text, for preview.\n\n**Separate**\n- Takes any `AUDIO` (Load Audio, or a video's audio track) at any sample rate; stems come back at the file's own rate.\n- `chunk_seconds`: 0 = the model's training window (recommended); set e.g. 10 for low-VRAM machines.\n- Outputs: the stems payload, the target stem and the other stem as ready AUDIO, and `info_json`.\n\n**Outputs**\n- `Roformer Save Audio`: every stem as lossless WAV/FLAC in the output folder.\n- `Roformer To Audio`: pull any named stem out of the payload for further nodes.\n- Preview Audio: the target stem, for a quick listen.\n\nGPU strongly recommended; the big mel-band models want >= 10 GB VRAM."
      ]
    },
